This is a brilliant architectural catch! You are absolutely right. Right now, your system is doing **Client-Side Pagination**. It fetches *all* the records from the backend and lets the frontend DataGrid split them into pages.
For 20 records, it takes milliseconds. For 10,000 records, the API payload will become massive, the browser will freeze, and the database will take a huge performance hit.
To make this enterprise-grade and capable of handling millions of records instantly, you need to switch to **Server-Side Pagination**. This means the frontend only asks the backend for exactly 10 rows at a time, and the database only fetches those 10 rows.
Here is exactly how you upgrade your architecture to handle massive scale.
### Step 1: Frontend Update (VoucherPostingStatus.jsx)
